[Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  20-17 is in full gear new releases is  still bringing you the hottest games and  this week is packed with heavy hitters  don't forget to hit that subscribe  button to keep up with all the titles  you don't want to miss now let's get to  it shall we the survival horror  juggernaut is back with resident evil 7  biohazard this time around the scares  are all up in your face thanks to a new  first-person perspective if you play the  demo you'll already be familiar with  solving puzzles swinging axes and firing  guns from your new point of view for the  rest of you this is a chance to explore  an all-new still creepy mansion owned by  the bizarre Baker family and if you've  got a PlayStation VR headset you'll be  able to confront them face-to-face  resident evil 7 hits ps4 xbox one and pc  on Tuesday January 24th the second game  this week is based on a literal heavy  hitter Don Bradman was the greatest  cricket batter of all time and his game  series is coming to pc with don bradman  cricket 17 the improved career mode lets  you start playing cricket locally before  sending the ranks to become a true  professional and as you make your way up  team line-ups will change thanks to  injuries retirement sand trades for the  first time you can also create your own  stadium don bradman cricket 17 hit  consoles late last year but you can grab  it for pc on the 22nd kingdom hearts HD  2.8 final chapter prologue is a mouthful  and much like the title its content is  also pretty stuffed the game includes an  HD remaster of dream Drop Distance the  first time you'll be able to play it on  anything other than the 3ds it also  contains an epilogue to birth by Sleep  called a fragmentary passage and Kingdom  Hearts key back cover a new story told  through cinematics this final collection  bridges the gap to kingdom hearts 3 so  expect to come away with just as many  questions as answers you can dive in on  ps4 on the 24th  speaking of big RPG series the tales  franchise is back with tales of Bruce  area the new game is set in the same  world as tales of zestiria but told many  years before lead hero velvet crow and  her party must battle the demon blight  using the series trademark linear motion  battle system that means real-time  combat where you can fight using weapons  magic spells and special skills called  arts if that sounds up your alley then  you can check out tales of Bruce area on  ps4 ps3 and pc on the 24th and finally  there's another franchise getting a new  entry Yakuza 0 is a prequel to the whole  gang of titles and it's finally  releasing worldwide this time  protagonist Kazuma Kiryu and goro majima  find themselves in the middle of a power  struggle between several different mobs  you'll still get the same helping of  minigames missions and street brawls but  this time your heroes can use three  different fighting styles when taking on  a group of thugs the more you battle the  stronger you'll become and the more  money you'll shake down during street  fights Yakuza 0 hits ps4 on the 24th but  you can check out our review on gamespot  right now and those are the big games  will be playing this week as always  remember that release dates are based on  retailer listings and are subject to  change thanks for watching guys I'll see  you next week  [Music]

